  id: Flexor_carpi_radialis_muscle.L
  partName: Flexor_carpi_radialis_muscle.L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The flexor carpi radialis is responsible for flexing the wrist joint and assisting
    in controlled limb movement. It plays an important role in stabilizing the joint
    during various activities, including weight-bearing and locomotion. '
  - This muscle works in coordination with other flexors to ensure smooth and controlled
    wrist motion. It also contributes to maintaining proper limb posture and alignment.
    Its function is essential for precise control and efficient movement of the forelimb.
